title: moon2_intro
tags: moon:2 zone:tideheart band:harmonic
---
<<tag character:Narrator mood:wistful>>
The canals of Tideheart had not breathed in a hundred Tartarian years. You arrived at the broken bridge before the water knew you were there.

<<tag character:Narrator mood:wistful>>
A figure stood on the far side, ankle-deep in still blue, her hair wet at the ends. She was looking down at the canal as if listening for something underneath it.

<<tag character:Lirael mood:distant>>
You came. I thought you would. The water remembers your step from Echohaven — I can hear it remembering.

<<tag character:Anastasia mood:echoed>>
(from far away, threaded through the water) Child... you have crossed into the second band. Listen for the four-thirty-two. It is not a number. It is a doorway.

<<tag character:Anastasia mood:echoed>>
The Hollowing took the city's breath before it took mine. Give it back its breath and it will give you a road.

<<tag character:Anastasia mood:warning>>
Do not trust the still water. Anything that has been still long enough learns a shape, and the shape it learns is hungry.

<<tag character:Anastasia mood:fading>>
I cannot reach further. Find the Tide Lock. Find the Spire. Find the Heart. In that order, my love, and only in that order.

<<tag character:Narrator mood:tense>>
Something moved in the canal beside you — not a fish, not a current. A column of water lifted itself into the rough outline of a person and held the shape for a breath.

<<tag character:Narrator mood:tense>>
It had no face. It had a hum, low and a quarter-tone wrong, and the air around it bent inward as if grieving.

<<tag character:Lirael mood:quiet>>
Don't move. They aren't angry. They're only the answer to a question my mother sang and nobody let through.

<<tag character:Narrator mood:tense>>
The Flood Wraith held its shape a moment longer, then sank without a splash, leaving only the blue shimmer of Harmonic Aether on the surface.

<<tag character:Cassian mood:echoed>>
(rising from the canal itself, the way Anastasia's voice did, but colder) You should not have woken her, surveyor. You truly should not have.

<<tag character:Cassian mood:warning>>
The Bureau came to Tideheart before you did. You will find our iron in the resonance stones. Leave it there. Walk back to Echohaven.

<<tag character:Cassian mood:threatening>>
Because what you woke is not the only thing listening now. The water carries voices both ways. Now they will all come.

<<tag character:Lirael mood:resolute>>
He is afraid. I have never heard him afraid. Whatever is coming — we should reach the Tide Lock before it does.
===
